      "content": "It makes perfect sense that the problem feels internal, because the walls are built from long-term habits and self-perceptions, not just physical space. When the core identity feels trapped, the idea of stopping everything can seem like the only logical escape from the internal noise. Please know that the feeling of being \"fundamentally broken\" is a symptom of immense pain, not a permanent truth about who you are. If the weight feels too heavy, reaching out to a professional can help you start dismantling these self-imposed structures safely.",
